{"id":"mahabharata-3-229","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":229,"title":"एकोनत्रिंशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 229 · The Gandharvas bar the way","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana inspects his herds and enjoys the forest, then orders a pleasure camp to be built by the Dvaita lake. His men find the lake occupied by the Gandharva king Chitrasena, who forbids them entry, and they hurry back to Duryodhana.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನು ಗೋವುಗಳನ್ನು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ ಕಾಡಿನಲ್ಲಿ ವಿಹರಿಸಿ ದ್ವೈತಸರೋವರದ ಬಳಿ ವಿಹಾರಶಿಬಿರ ಕಟ್ಟಲು ಆಜ್ಞಾಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವನ ಜನರು ಸರೋವರವನ್ನು ಗಂಧರ್ವರಾಜ ಚಿತ್ರಸೇನನು ಆಕ್ರಮಿಸಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅವನು ಪ್ರವೇಶ ನಿಷೇಧಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವರು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಬಳಿ ಓಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन अपने पशुओं का निरीक्षण कर वन का आनन्द लेता है, फिर द्वैत सरोवर के पास विहार-शिविर बनाने का आदेश देता है। उसके लोग पाते हैं कि सरोवर पर गन्धर्वराज चित्रसेन ठहरे हैं, जो उन्हें प्रवेश से रोकते हैं, और वे दुर्योधन के पास लौट जाते हैं।","te":"దుర్యోధనుడు గోవులను పరిశీలించి అడవిలో విహరించి ద్వైతసరస్సు దగ్గర విహారశిబిరం నిర్మించమని ఆజ్ఞాపిస్తాడు. అతని మనుషులు సరస్సు వద్ద గంధర్వరాజు చిత్రసేనుడు ఉన్నాడని చూస్తారు; అతడు ప్రవేశం నిషేధిస్తాడు, వారు దుర్యోధనుని దగ్గరకు పరుగెత్తుతారు.","ta":"துரியோதனன் தன் மந்தைகளைப் பார்வையிட்டுக் காட்டில் இன்புற்று, த்வைத ஏரியருகே உல்லாசப் பாசறை அமைக்க ஆணையிடுகிறான். அவன் ஆட்கள் ஏரியைக் கந்தர்வ அரசன் சித்ரஸேனன் ஆக்கிரமித்திருப்பதைக் காண, அவன் நுழையத் தடை விதிக்க, அவர்கள் துரியோதனனிடம் விரைகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനൻ തന്റെ കന്നുകാലികളെ പരിശോധിച്ച് കാടിന്റെ ഭംഗി ആസ്വദിക്കുന്നു; പിന്നെ ദ്വൈതതടാകത്തിനരികെ ഒരു ആനന്ദപാളയം പണിയാൻ കൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു. പക്ഷേ തടാകത്തിൽ ഗന്ധർവരാജാവായ ചിത്രസേനൻ ഉണ്ടെന്നും അവർ പ്രവേശനം വിലക്കുന്നുവെന്നും ആളുകൾ കണ്ടെത്തി, തിരിച്ച് ദുര്യോധനന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് ഓടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.229; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"घोषयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Ghoshayatra Parva (The cattle expedition)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथ दुर्योधनो राजा तत्र तत्र वने वसन् ।\nजगाम घोषानभितस्तत्र चक्रे निवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"King Duryodhana, staying here and there in the forest, went around the cattle stations and set up camp there.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"रमणीये समाज्ञाते सोदके समहीरुहे ।\nदेशे सर्वगुणोपेते चक्रुरावसथं नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In a delightful, well-known place with water and trees, endowed with every good quality, men built a dwelling.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"तथैव तत्समीपस्थान्पृथगावसथान्बहून् ।\nकर्णस्य शकुनेश्चैव भ्रातॄणां चैव सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Likewise, many separate dwellings nearby were built for Karna, for Shakuni and for all his brothers.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"ददर्श स तदा गावः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nअङ्कैर्लक्षैश्च ताः सर्वा लक्षयामास पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then he saw cattle by the hundred and thousand, and the king had all of them marked with signs and brands.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"अङ्कयामास वत्सांश्च जज्ञे चोपसृतास्त्वपि ।\nबालवत्साश्च या गावः कालयामास ता अपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He had the calves branded and noted those that had come near; he also had the cows with young calves driven along.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अथ स स्मारणं कृत्वा लक्षयित्वा त्रिहायनान् ।\nवृतो गोपालकैः प्रीतो व्यहरत्कुरुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"After the counting and noting the three-year-olds, the delighted Kuru scion roamed, surrounded by the cowherds.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"स च पौरजनः सर्वः सैनिकाश्च सहस्रशः ।\nयथोपजोषं चिक्रीडुर्वने तस्मिन्यथामराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All the townspeople and thousands of soldiers sported in that forest as they pleased, like immortals.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो गोपाः प्रगातारः कुशला नृत्तवादिते ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रमुपातिष्ठन्कन्याश्चैव स्वलंकृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then cowherds skilled in singing, dancing and playing, and richly adorned girls, came to Dhritarashtra's son.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"स स्त्रीगणवृतो राजा प्रहृष्टः प्रददौ वसु ।\nतेभ्यो यथार्हमन्नानि पानानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The king, surrounded by troops of women and very pleased, gave them wealth, and suitable food and various drinks.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"ततस्ते सहिताः सर्वे तरक्षून्महिषान्मृगान् ।\nगवयर्क्षवराहांश्च समन्तात्पर्यकालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then all together they drove around hyenas, buffaloes, deer, gayals, bears and wild boars from every side.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"स ताञ्शरैर्विनिर्भिन्दन्गजान्बध्नन्महावने ।\nरमणीयेषु देशेषु ग्राहयामास वै मृगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He pierced them with arrows and captured elephants in that great forest, and had deer caught in pleasant places.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"गोरसानुपयुञ्जान उपभोगांश्च भारत ।\nपश्यन्सुरमणीयानि पुष्पितानि वनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Enjoying the milk and other comforts, descendant of Bharata, seeing the lovely blossoming forests...\""}},{"n":13,"text":"मत्तभ्रमरजुष्टानि बर्हिणाभिरुतानि च ।\nअगच्छदानुपूर्व्येण पुण्यं द्वैतवनं सरः ।\nऋद्ध्या परमया युक्तो महेन्द्र इव वज्रभृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"filled with intoxicated bees and resounding with peacocks, he went in due course to the holy lake of Dvaitavana, endowed with supreme splendor like Mahendra, wielder of the thunderbolt.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"यदृच्छया च तदहो धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nईजे राजर्षियज्ञेन सद्यस्केन विशां पते ।\nदिव्येन विधिना राजा वन्येन कुरुसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By chance on that day Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, was performing a royal-sage's sacrifice, a one-day rite, king, in the divine manner of the forest.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"कृत्वा निवेशमभितः सरसस्तस्य कौरवः ।\nद्रौपद्या सहितो धीमान्धर्मपत्न्या नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The wise king, a Kuru, with Draupadi, his wife in dharma, had made a camp on all sides of that lake.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनः प्रेष्यानादिदेश सहानुजः ।\nआक्रीडावसथाः क्षिप्रं क्रियन्तामिति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then Duryodhana with his younger brothers ordered his servants, 'Quickly make pleasure houses.'\""}},{"n":17,"text":"ते तथेत्येव कौरव्यमुक्त्वा वचनकारिणः ।\nचिकीर्षन्तस्तदाक्रीडाञ्जग्मुर्द्वैतवनं सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They said 'So be it' to the Kaurava, obeying his word, and went to the lake of Dvaitavana, wishing to build the pleasure grounds.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"सेनाग्रं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य प्राप्तं द्वैतवनं सरः ।\nप्रविशन्तं वनद्वारि गन्धर्वाः समवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The front of Dhritarashtra's son's army reached Dvaitavana lake, and as it entered at the gate of the forest, gandharvas stopped it.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्र गन्धर्वराजो वै पूर्वमेव विशां पते ।\nकुबेरभवनाद्राजन्नाजगाम गणावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The king of the gandharvas had already come from Kubera's palace, king, surrounded by his troops.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"गणैरप्सरसां चैव त्रिदशानां तथात्मजैः ।\nविहारशीलः क्रीडार्थं तेन तत्संवृतं सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With troops of apsarases and the sons of the gods, fond of play, he had the lake surrounded for his sport.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तेन तत्संवृतं दृष्ट्वा ते राजपरिचारकाः ।\nप्रतिजग्मुस्ततो राजन्यत्र दुर्योधनो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Seeing it occupied by him, the king's attendants returned, king, to where King Duryodhana was.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"स तु तेषां वचः श्रुत्वा सैनिकान्युद्धदुर्मदान् ।\nप्रेषयामास कौरव्य उत्सारयत तानिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing their words, he sent soldiers who were arrogant for battle, saying, 'Drive them away.'\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा राज्ञः सेनाग्रयायिनः ।\nसरो द्वैतवनं गत्वा गन्धर्वानिदमब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing his words, the king's vanguard went to Dvaitavana lake and said this to the gandharvas.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"राजा दुर्योधनो नाम धृतराष्ट्रसुतो बली ।\nविजिहीर्षुरिहायाति तदर्थमपसर्पत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The mighty King Duryodhana, Dhritarashtra's son, comes here wishing to amuse himself. Move away for his sake.'\""}},{"n":25,"text":"एवमुक्तास्तु गन्धर्वाः प्रहसन्तो विशां पते ।\nप्रत्यब्रुवंस्तान्पुरुषानिदं सुपरुषं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So addressed, the gandharvas, laughing, answered those men with these very harsh words, lord of the people.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"न चेतयति वो राजा मन्दबुद्धिः सुयोधनः ।\nयोऽस्मानाज्ञापयत्येवं वश्यानिव दिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Your king Suyodhana has no sense, a dull-witted man, who orders us, gods in heaven, as if we were his subjects.'\""}},{"n":27,"text":"यूयं मुमूर्षवश्चापि मन्दप्रज्ञा न संशयः ।\nये तस्य वचनादेवमस्मान्ब्रूत विचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You are bent on death, without doubt, and dull of wit, you senseless men, who speak to us like this at his word.'\""}},{"n":28,"text":"गच्छत त्वरिताः सर्वे यत्र राजा स कौरवः ।\nद्वेष्यं माद्यैव गच्छध्वं धर्मराजनिवेशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Go quickly, all of you, to where that Kaurava king is. Do not go today to the dwelling of the hateful Dharmaraja.'\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एवमुक्तास्तु गन्धर्वै राज्ञः सेनाग्रयायिनः ।\nसंप्राद्रवन्यतो राजा धृतराष्ट्रसुतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Told so by the gandharvas, the king's vanguard ran back to where Dhritarashtra's son was.\""}}]}]}